network-guide.md:17: - `PerformanceInterceptor` - Optional HTTP timing (when performance service is wired). The path it records - trace name and `http_path` attribute - goes through `ApiLoggingInterceptor.redactPath` first, so a `?token=` in a path is redacted there exactly as in the logs
network-guide.md:354: - `RawWebSocketClientImpl`: Concrete class powered by the `web_socket_channel` package. Its handshake follows the same pinning policy as `ApiClient`: when pinning is in effect it connects through the pinned `HttpClient` from `SslPinning.createHttpClient()`, so a `wss://` server whose certificate the fingerprints do not name is refused. Pass `sslPinning:` to use a different policy. Its log lines and every error `connect` throws name the URL redacted - userinfo and query values whose key names a secret replaced - so a realtime token does not reach a crash report. In a staging or production release, `connect` refuses any URL that is not `wss://` (a `WebSocketChannelException`, nothing opened), as `main()` refuses a non-`https` `BASE_URL`; development, debug and profile builds still accept `ws://`. The same release refuses a handshake redirect that leaves TLS (a `wss://` server answering `302 -> http://...`), which dart:io would otherwise follow into cleartext; a redirect to another `https` URL is followed, pinned as the first hop is.
